//! Minimal HTTP surface for the editor MVP (P1-d step 1) + task-bundle save
//! routes (N3). Since PR1 this module hosts BOTH product surfaces (design
//! `docs/RUNNER-STUDIO-SPLIT-PLAN.md` §A.2/§A.3):
//!
//! * `Surface::Studio` (`oasd studio`, default port 8788): editor/builder APIs,
//!   `ui/index.html`;
//! * `Surface::Runner` (`oasd runner`, default port 8789): usage/runtime APIs,
//!   `ui/runner.html`;
//! * shared read-only routes (`GET /instance`, `GET /stats`, `GET /runs`, ...)
//!   work on both. [`required_surface`] is the authoritative pure-function gate
//!   applied in [`Server::handle`] before any handler runs.
//!
//! Deliberately std::net only: the UI is plain static HTML/JS, so the exact same
//! files can later be wrapped by Tauri (desktop) or a WebView shell (Android)
//! without changes. JSON is handled with `serde_json` (the only new dependency).
//!
//! Routes:
//!   GET  /                -> ui/index.html (Studio) | ui/runner.html (Runner)
//!   GET  /app.js          -> ui/app.js (Studio only)
//!   GET  /runner.js       -> ui/runner.js (Runner only)
//!   GET  /frame.png       -> last captured frame (404 before the first capture)
//!   POST /capture         -> capture a fresh frame, returns JSON {width,height}
//!   GET  /state           -> JSON {captured, width, height, device, ocr, det}
//!   POST /input/tap       -> live-preview passthrough: tap current device
//!   POST /input/swipe     -> live-preview passthrough: swipe current device
//!   GET  /ocr?x&y&w&h     -> single-line OCR
//!   GET  /lines?x&y&w&h   -> multi-line det+rec
//!   POST /task/save_asset -> crop the LAST captured frame -> task bundle
//!   GET  /task/assets?task=Name -> assets.json summary
//!   POST /task/save_flow  -> validate + save flow.json (asset refs checked)
//!   GET  /task/list       -> task bundle names under --tasks-dir
//!   POST /task/create     -> atomically create a new task bundle skeleton (N38/M1)
//!   POST /task/run        -> run a task bundle in the background via `run::execute`
//!   GET  /task/run/status -> status/log tail of the current or last editor run
//!   GET  /runs            -> click-run JSONL files under --runs-dir (§21 CD1/CD4)
//!   GET  /runs/clicks?file=<name> -> one run's CD2 click rows (§21 CD2/CD3)
//!   GET  /runs/scheduler?limit=&task=&outcome= -> P4 scheduler run entities (list)
//!   GET  /runs/scheduler/run?run_id=<id>       -> one P4 scheduler run entity
//!   GET  /runner/health   -> Runner health JSON (Runner only, PR1)
//!   GET  /runner/tasks    -> Runner task listing JSON (Runner only, PR1; PR5 adds installed info)
//!   GET  /runner/packages -> installed.json registry + unmanaged tasks (PR5)
//!   POST /runner/install  -> install a local .oaspkg path (PR5, path mode)
//!   POST /runner/uninstall / /runner/packages/activate (PR5)
//!   GET  /runner/scheduler/status  -> embedded scheduler state (Runner only, PR6)
//!   POST /runner/scheduler/start|stop -> start/stop the embedded thread (PR6)
//!   POST /runner/run      -> temporary Runner run (values.json + body params, PR6)
//!   GET  /runner/run/status -> status of the current/last temporary run (PR6)
//!   GET  /runner/tasks/<id>/config  -> Runner task values + input variables (V2.0b)
//!   PUT  /runner/tasks/<id>/config  -> validate + store Runner-editable input values
//!   GET  /runner/updates  -> publish events from the exchange dir + update feeds (P0-1a/P2)
//!   POST /runner/updates/ack -> Runner-local seen state (`dismissed`/`installed`, P0-1a)
//!   POST /runner/updates/install -> install one update event (downloads URL packages; P2)
//!   POST /runner/updates/cache/clear -> drop cached feed indexes + remote packages (P2)
//!   POST /runner/notify   -> best-effort publish hint (never installs; P0-1a)
//!   POST /task/publish    -> build one .oaspkg (Studio only, PR5)
//!   GET  /task/package    -> Studio package history (PR5)
//!   GET  /task/lint?task=<name> -> authoritative task lint report (Studio only, P2)
//!   GET  /task/variables?task=<name> -> Studio V2 variable schema (V2.0b)
//!   POST /task/variables             -> Studio saves `meta.variables` (V2.0b;
//!                                       the old `/task/config` is a deprecated alias)
//!   GET  /task/config?task=<name>   -> Studio param schema (PR2, deprecated alias)
//!   POST /task/config               -> Studio edits `meta.params` (PR2, deprecated alias)
//!
//! Validation failures answer `400` with a structured `{"ok":false,"errors":[...]}`.

